# Constraint violation: + requires Number for both arguments.
# x@Int satisfies Number, but "hello" (String) does not.
# The type checker reports a unification error when checking the String argument.
# Eval proceeds — the function body is never invoked so no runtime error occurs.
# Note: builtin-concat is private (not in user scope); this tests the same category
# of numeric constraint violation via the public + operator.
[f: [fn [let x@Int] [+ x "hello"]]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x)})

=== warn
no instance for Addable Int String
